# SRG-APP-000095-AU-000050  -  CAT III
# The System Administrator (SA) and Information System Security Manager
# (ISSM) must configure the retention of the log records based on
# criticality level, event type, and/or retention period, at a minimum.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations, then kept
# by hand. Edit this file to change how this requirement is assessed here;
# it is read at run time. Regenerating refreshes the benchmark text in place
# and leaves the criteria, the determination and any verification block as
# they are.

id:              SRG-APP-000095-AU-000050
group:           V-241819
severity:        low
cat:             CAT III
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      derived
revised:         yes
cci:             CCI-001914 CCI-000130
control_rev5:    AU-12 AU-3

contribution:    Splunk sets retention per index: frozenTimePeriodInSecs is the retention
                 period in seconds, so the product can express whatever period the
                 organization documents.

governs:         indexes.conf - The indexes data is stored in, how large they may grow and how long data
                 is kept.

check:           indexes.conf [] frozenTimePeriodInSecs present

external:        The documented retention period, criticality levels and event types are
                 organization-defined; SPLK-CL-000120 compares frozenTimePeriodInSecs
                 against the site documentation, which the application cannot supply.
external:        Assignment of the SA and ISSM to a Splunk role that holds indexes_edit is
                 account provisioning and ISSM appointment; authorize.conf records a role's
                 capabilities, not who holds the role.

citation:        DIRECTION, inverted. Removed authorize.conf [role_user] indexes_edit
                 absent. The check text reads "Verify the SA and ISSM have been assigned
                 the privileges needed to allow these roles to change the level and type of
                 log records that are retained", and CCI-001914 is a provision requirement
                 - the capability must exist for the named roles. Withholding indexes_edit
                 from the ordinary user role is the opposite test, and it passes vacuously
                 anyway: the shipped [role_user] in system/default/authorize.conf does not
                 list indexes_edit, so the condition reports compliant without any evidence
                 that the required privilege exists. A positive condition is not a sound
                 replacement either, because authorize.conf.spec accepts only "enabled" for
                 a capability and the product ships indexes_edit = enabled under
                 [role_admin], so such a condition could never fail. The privilege question
                 is therefore recorded as an external dependency.
finding:         No retention period is expressed for the indexes in scope
                 (frozenTimePeriodInSecs is not set), so the retention the organization
                 documented by criticality level, event type and period is not configured
                 in the product.
